    thinking: "**Defining App Identity**\n\nOkay, I\'m defining the application\'s identity. I\'ve got the title, \"Dean Wilshaw Web Development,\" from `metadata.json`. The description is set: \"High-performance bespoke websites and custom React builds for local business growth in Cheshire and Stoke.\" This foundational information is complete and confirmed.\n\n\n**Developing Server-Side Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the full-stack Express + Vite server. The `server.ts` is running on port 3000, handling the `/api/chat` route using the Gemini API for the \"Stitch Support\" AI assistant, including a detailed system prompt defining its role. I\'ve also set up `/api/quote` for project estimates and `/api/speed-test` for web vitals comparison. I\'ve updated `package.json` scripts as well.\n\n\n**Constructing Frontend Layout**\n\nI\'m currently building out the frontend. I\'ve designed a responsive header with navigation, including a logo, services menu, and a call-to-action quote button. The hero section is next, with a \"Engineered for Performance\" badge and a strong title highlighting fast websites for business growth. I\'m focusing on calls to action (Get a Quote and WhatsApp messaging). I\'m also preparing for an interactive code/preview showcase to highlight performance.\n\n\n**Refining Key Selling Points**\n\nI\'m now refining the core value propositions. I am highlighting single-page applications built with React and Vite. I\'ve ensured a lead-generation focus with a strategic UI/UX design. I\'ve also incorporated modern technical SEO techniques. I am now incorporating operational analytics for lead tracking. I am preparing clickable cards with technical specs and ROI metrics. I\'m adding an interactive speed test with a benchmark calculator, and finally a comparison table to highlight the advantages of custom builds.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Business Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating priority features. I\'m building an interactive timeline illustrating the engineering roadmap, broken down into key steps. An \"About\" section is being implemented, highlighting my logistics background with an interactive stats counter. I\'m finalizing a \"Request a Quote\" form with an integrated calculator for pricing and timelines, complete with instant submission and contact options. Finally, the \"Stitch Support\" chatbot is added with a floating button and notification.\n\n\n**Integrating Conversational Features**\n\nI\'ve integrated a powerful real-time AI chat powered by the Gemini API at `/api/chat`, complete with fallback quick-prompt buttons. I\'ve also added the ability to request a quote directly within the chat interface. I\'m also now building out a styled modal with a pre-configured WhatsApp message generator.\n\nI\'m now integrating a simple footer with copyright, a Cheshire badge, and social media/contact links to connect via WhatsApp, email, LinkedIn, and GitHub.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 896494161
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
